2026-09-27T07:58:44.3110951Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3111446Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3111914Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3113030Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3114131Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3114225Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3114430Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3114709Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3114962Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3115321Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3115623Z ================
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3115740Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3115901Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3116266Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3116484Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3116594Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3116857Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3117179Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3117318Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3117706Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3118036Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3118656Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3119148Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3119252Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3119673Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3120204Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3120477Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3120767Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3121146Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3121234Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3121424Z ========
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3121528Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3122743Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3123999Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3124208Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3124663Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3197769Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3198637Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3199229Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3199671Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3200140Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3200245Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3200519Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3200663Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3201704Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3202824Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3203447Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3204253Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:58:44.3204482Z 
